<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wadiyar dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1399–1950</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Wodeyar dynasty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Wodeyar or Wadiyar dynasty ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mysore">Mysore</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, by tradition from 1399 until after Indian independence. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">Vassals</a> of Vijayanagara at first, they became independent after Raja Wodeyar I took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srirangapatna">Srirangapatna</a> in 1610. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyder-ali">Hyder Ali</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tipu-sultan">Tipu Sultan</a> held real power from 1761, but the British restored the Wodeyars in 1799, and they ruled the princely state until 1950.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wadiyar-dynasty.jpg" alt="Wadiyar dynasty" width="320" height="325" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rustyshackelford · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Royal_coat_of_arms_of_the_Kingdom_of_Mysore.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
